-- =====================================================================
-- 0090 · EMILY (TL-053-26, v2): A PRIMEIRA FOLHA, COMPLETA
--
-- Instrução dela, nov/26, sobre a 0089: a descrição não é uma linha por
-- dia. É a do briefing, adaptada: primeiro os voos, depois transfers e
-- transporte, depois o que a TL sugere, dia a dia, com o texto inteiro.
--
-- Adaptado às respostas da Danielle (8/11):
--   · onde o briefing dava duas opções, fica só a escolhida — 27/6 é o
--     Chianti, Lucca sai;
--   · Arezzo: a peça feita para a Emily, colar ou pulseira;
--   · 2/7: "Luxury Shopping Experience" para o casal, e no fim do dia,
--     como opção, o jantar privado numa residência histórica. A visita ao
--     Palazzo Doria Pamphilj SAI, por instrução dela;
--   · "A Customer Journey with Destinations by Dani" fica inteira, e o
--     antes da viagem passa a sugerir um concierge opcional para seleção,
--     agendamento e reserva dos restaurantes de todos os dias, antes do
--     embarque.
--
-- Sai, por ser execução prometida antes de cotar (regra da 0062): "we
-- select an estate", "we take care of everything around the drive",
-- "we will suggest", "we will look at proposing". Fica o que a
-- experiência É e o que é oferecido como opção.
--
-- Mexe só na v2, guardado: só troca se a folha ainda for a da 0089.
-- Seção 7: ops_proposals (update na v2), ops_migrations (insert).
-- =====================================================================

with t(d) as (select E'Emily and Nathan land in Florence on Sunday, June 20, and fly home from Rome on Saturday, July 3. Thirteen nights in three bases, five in Cortona, four at Castelfalfi and four in Rome.\n\nFLIGHTS\nBusiness class, booked by Fora, Delta reservation F8SCB6.\n- Sat, Jun 19: DL 9219, operated by KLM · Portland 1:05pm to Amsterdam 7:40am, Jun 20\n- Sun, Jun 20: DL 9388, operated by KLM Cityhopper · Amsterdam 9:30am to Florence 11:30am\n- Sat, Jul 3: DL 325 · Rome Fiumicino, Terminal 3, 12:20pm to Seattle 3:30pm\n- Sat, Jul 3: DL 3913 · Seattle 5:40pm to Portland 6:43pm\nThey clear passport control in Amsterdam, so the landing in Florence works like a domestic arrival and they are out quickly.\n\nTRANSFERS AND TRANSPORT\n- Arrival: a private transfer from Florence airport to the palace in Cortona, about 1h30, so the first drive after the long flight is one they don''t have to make themselves.\n- In Tuscany: a midsize BMW or Mercedes SUV, or similar, delivered to them in Cortona on the morning of June 21, at the parking lot a few minutes from the palace. It stays with them through the Castelfalfi days.\n- To Rome: on June 29 the Tuscan car is collected at Castelfalfi and a Ferrari takes its place for the drive to Rome. Near Rome they hand over the keys and continue with a private transfer, while their luggage travels ahead to the hotel.\n- In Rome: no car is needed. On the days with experiences, a private car picks them up at the hotel.\n- Departure: a private transfer from the hotel to Fiumicino, Terminal 3, on July 3.\nThe plan assumes they drive the rental car in Tuscany. On the days built around a winery or a long lunch, a driver can be arranged if they''d like, so they can enjoy the table without thinking about the road back.\n\nOUR SUGGESTIONS, DAY BY DAY\n\nCORTONA · JUNE 20 TO 25\nCortona is a hilltop town in the Val di Chiana, in the south of Tuscany, right at the border with Umbria. From here every direction leads somewhere worth the drive, and the days are made for taking it slowly.\nSunday, June 20 · Arrival: the transfer brings them to the palace in the early afternoon, with time to rest and settle in. Later, an easy first walk through Cortona at their own pace, its steep lanes and piazzas, with the Val di Chiana opening below the town walls. For dinner, a trattoria in town for a first taste of the local cooking.\nMonday, June 21 · Montalcino and its wine: the car is delivered in the morning, and the day goes to Montalcino, home of Brunello di Montalcino, one of the most prestigious wines in Italy. An estate with a complete experience, a visit and lunch, for a couple who enjoy the setting and the food as much as the wine.\nTuesday, June 22 · Montepulciano and Pienza: two of the most beautiful towns of southern Tuscany, in the landscape of cypress lines and golden hills that most people picture when they think of Tuscany. Part of the charm is simply discovering them, their lanes, piazzas and views over the valley. Lunch in the area, at a farm-to-table restaurant serving the local cooking.\nWednesday, June 23 · Arezzo and the goldsmith: Arezzo has been a city of goldsmiths for centuries, and it is about 30 minutes from Cortona. The day combines the city and its Piazza Grande with time in a goldsmith''s workshop, to shape a piece made especially for Emily, a necklace or a bracelet, simple and elegant, to complete an outfit.\nThursday, June 24 · A day of their own: a free day to enjoy the palace and the area at their own pace. If they feel like exploring further, Umbria is very close, with Orvieto standing on its rock, or the small town of Deruta, famous for its ceramics.\n\nCASTELFALFI · JUNE 25 TO 29\nLate June is one of the loveliest moments to be outdoors in Tuscany, so these days lean on what the region does best, food, wine and the countryside. There is time to enjoy the resort, and most activities are planned so they are back by late afternoon.\nFriday, June 25 · Cortona to Castelfalfi: about 1h45 on the road, straight to Castelfalfi, with the afternoon free to settle in and enjoy the resort.\nSaturday, June 26 · Truffles and the countryside: truffle hunting is part of life in these hills. In the morning they head into the woods with a truffle hunter and his dogs, followed by a lunch with truffles. The afternoon is free at the resort. For dinner, an evening outdoors among the vineyards, or at Castelfalfi itself.\nSunday, June 27 · The Chianti: a day in the Chianti, the hills between Florence and Siena, among wine estates and hilltop villages.\nMonday, June 28 · Last day in Tuscany: a slow morning at the resort. In the afternoon a vintage car is waiting for them, for a drive through the surrounding hills and a picnic along the way.\n\nROME · JUNE 29 TO JULY 3\nThe days below are a suggestion. Each experience is placed according to availability, once the logistics are confirmed.\nTuesday, June 29 · Castelfalfi to Rome, behind the wheel: in the morning the Tuscan car stays behind and a Ferrari is waiting for them at the door. The road ahead is theirs, curves through the hills, rows of cypress, villages on the ridges, and then the light opening up toward the sea. The route is designed for them, with a stretch along the coast or a stop in a village on the way. Near Rome they hand over the keys and continue with a private transfer. In the evening, check-in at the Bulgari Hotel Roma.\nWednesday, June 30 · The Colosseum: a day dedicated to the Colosseum. Since private access isn''t available, it starts with the underground, one of its most requested areas, where gladiators and animals waited before the games. It is visited in small groups at set times, ideally at the first slot of the day, when it is quieter. From there their guide takes them through the rest of the Colosseum and on to the Roman Forum. The afternoon is free to explore the centre of Rome at an easy pace.\nEach year the Colosseum sets aside a few dates for evening experiences. If one of them falls during their stay, it can be proposed as an option, keeping in mind that the next morning starts early.\nThursday, July 1 · The Vatican with the Clavigero: before the doors open to the public, the Vatican Museums are silent. Emily and Nathan wait at the main entrance with their private guide until the sound of keys announces the Clavigero, the keeper who opens the museums every morning. Door after door, he unlocks the rooms and turns on the lights. The afternoon is free to wander Rome at their own pace. At sunset, a luxury boat on the Tiber, to see Rome from the river as the light turns golden, with the stories of the places drifting by.\nFriday, July 2 · Luxury shopping and a last evening: a Luxury Shopping Experience for the two of them, in the boutiques around Via Condotti, a short walk from the hotel, with a personal shopper by their side. At the end of the day, as an option, a private dinner in a historic Roman residence, on a terrace over the rooftops of the city.\nSaturday, July 3 · Departure: a private transfer to Fiumicino, Terminal 3, for the 12:20 flight, leaving the hotel around 9:00.\n\nA CUSTOMER JOURNEY WITH DESTINATIONS BY DANI\nTuscan Lands is the trusted ground partner of Destinations by Dani in Italy. We coordinate the whole trip locally, from the stays to every transfer and experience, in direct contact with Danielle at every step.\n- Before the trip: we suggest an optional concierge service for the selection, booking and reservation of the restaurants for all these days, arranged before departure.\n- During the trip: our team on the ground follows the journey day by day, always together with Danielle.'::text)
update ops_proposals set curations = jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
    'cor', 'verde', 'opcao', '',
    'title_en', 'Emily & Nathan · Tuscany and Rome',
    'title_pt', 'Emily & Nathan · Tuscany and Rome',
    'dest_en',  E'Florence · Cortona · Castelfalfi · Rome\nJune 20 to July 3, 2027 · 13 nights',
    'dest_pt',  E'Florence · Cortona · Castelfalfi · Rome\nJune 20 to July 3, 2027 · 13 nights',
    'dias_en', (select d from t),
    'dias_pt', (select d from t)))
 where id = 'e0530000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002'
   and responded_at is null
   and curations::text like '%DAY BY DAY%';

insert into ops_migrations (id) values ('0090-emily-v2-primeira-folha-completa') on conflict (id) do nothing;
